  "architecture": {
    "Overview": "The first mosque of Islam was the house of the Islamic prophet Mohammad in Medina. When it was first built by Muhammad and his companions, it was made of simple blocks. As time passed and different Muslim empires and rulers were honored to rule Medina, the mosque has been subjected to different constructions. The last construction was done by the different Saudi kings. The current construction is the prototype of all later sacred Islamic architecture."
